    "one_slot": "TestOperation times out at go test's 60s limit with the test goroutine at test_cluster_pool.go:109 called from nexus_otel_test.go:143"
  },
  "cause": "TestOperation needs two dedicated cluster slots at once. Under Gomad GOMAXPROCS is 1, so the dedicated pool has one slot unless TEMPORAL_TEST_DEDICATED_CLUSTERS overrides it. The Runner records --env entries and places them in the process environment, but the patched syscall.copyenv replaces the environment with TZ=UTC in deterministic mode (go1.27.1.patch:892-896), so the override never reaches testcore. The test takes the only slot and waits on a bare channel receive for a second one. The wait has no deadline, the cluster's periodic timers keep virtual time advancing, and the wall watchdog kills the target at a host-timed virtual instant. The first evidence field that differs between repetitions is virtual_time_elapsed_nanos, and the workload is classified nondeterministic; the comparison stops at the first mismatch, so a complete field comparison is not retained. A killed target writes no terminal choice frame, its artifact is replayed diagnostically without tracing, and the replay's stderr differs from a traced recording in one %p address.",
  "d12_d14": "no evidence of a shared cause. The D14 fix does not change the outcome: the recorded classification reproduces on toolchain 8d28bd44, which contains it. Supporting observations: stderr is byte-identical across repetitions up to the watchdog kill; with a virtual test timeout the failing run repeats byte for byte; with two real slots the suite qualifies with exact choice-tape replay. Not established: the killed runs keep no Choice Trace, so a choice divergence in them cannot be excluded from traces; the unfixed toolchain no longer exists, so no run compares the two; D12 is a linux/amd64 channel and is unassessed because no linux run exists.",
  "proposed_correction": {
    "recommended": "Deliver Runner-supplied environment entries to the target in deterministic mode (syscall.copyenv hunk of the runtime patch), with a conformance fixture; then set environment TEMPORAL_TEST_DEDICATED_CLUSTERS=2 on TestNexusOTELSuite in the generator manifest and remove the skip after verification",
    "owner": "Gomad runtime patch and Runner (tools/gomad3, owner gomad3)",
    "alternatives": [
      "Reject --env and the manifest environment field while the runtime hides them, and correct TUTORIAL.md and ARCHITECTURE.md",
      "Size the dedicated pool under the gomad build tag in tests/testcore (fn105-d17-variant-pool2.diff.txt shows the effect of two slots); owner gomad3 integration in tests/testcore"
    ],
    "state": "open work in fn-105 for a subsequent decision; nothing is implemented; the skip stays"
  },
